 one is rejected). It takes precedence over `orgPluginSettings` for that server in chat, Cowork and Code sessions alike; with no `toolPolicy` the server is left unrestricted. An entry whose name matches no installed plugin server does nothing.\n\nDesktop versions that predate `policy-only` do not recognise it: they drop the entry (listed under Configuration parse errors in the diagnostics report) and apply `orgPluginSettings` to that server instead. If every entry in the list is `policy-only`, those versions cannot read `managedMcpServers` at all: they report a parse error for it and, until they are updated, leave MCP servers that users added themselves, or that a project\'s `.mcp.json` declares, out of Code sessions. While older versions are still in use, keep the same permissions in `orgPluginSettings` too, and do not deploy a list made only of `policy-only` entries until every desktop has updated.'),nR=E.shortDescription(S.msg({defaultMessage:"Static headers sent on every request \u2014 routing and tenant headers only. No credentials here; use the headers helper script for tokens and rotating values.",id:"McpHeadersHint2"})),rR=E.shortDescription(S.msg({defaultMessage:"How long the helper\u2019s headers are reused before it runs again, in seconds. Defaults to 300.",id:"HtyK0/oE2w"})),iR=E.shortDescription(S.msg({defaultMessage:"Seconds before the TTL expires at which the helper re-runs mid-session. Defaults to 60. Keep it larger than the helper\u2019s typical runtime.",id:"zq1cbZBApQ"})),Mh=E.subfield(I.z.string().min(1),{label:S.msg({defaultMessage:"Name",id:"HAlOn1ZsuY"}),isPrimaryKey:!0,placeholder:S.msg({defaultMessage:"github",id:"Zejj2Gw5fy"}),description:{short:E.shortDescription(S.msg({defaultMessage:"Unique name for this server. Shown to users and used to key tool policy and sign-in state.",id:"40I9DtVbWB"}))}});is.PLUGIN_MCP_TOOL_POLICY_CHANNEL_NOTE=`For a plugin server that Claude Code launches or connects to itself (a marketplace plugin's), the permis